  "query_preview": "..\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nThe vertically stacked low over southern Alberta, SW Saskatchewan \nand northern Montana will remain rotate through eastern Montana\ntoday and tonight and move to Manitoba on Tuesday. A dry slot over\neastern Montana early this morning is expected to fill in with \nconvection during the day today as the upper low moves into the \narea and diminish tonight as the low moves to the northeast. As\nthe low exits the forecast area tonight, gusty west winds will\ndevelop with a Lake Wind Advisory likely for Fort Peck Lake on\nTuesday. There will be chances for more showers and thunderstorms\nas shortwaves move through NE Montana around the upper low to the\nNE. \n\nA broad upper trough will remain in place over western Canada and\nwestern US for the remainder of the week that will continue to\nbring chances for showers and thunderstorms every day.\nTemperatures will gradually warm through Friday. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nLow confidence on timing any showers and thunderstorms over the\nnext few days. High confidence on the warmer temperatures as the\nweek progress. No deviations from the NBM at this time.",
